Package: homelab-backup-client
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-yaml, borgbackup, openssh-client, homelab-cli
Recommends: python3-systemd
Conflicts: borgbackup2
Replaces: homelab-borg-service-backup-client, homelab-borg-service-backup
Breaks: homelab-borg-service-backup-client (<< 0.4.0), homelab-borg-service-backup (<< 0.2.0)
Description: Homelab backup client built on borg, homelab-api integrated
 Client-side backup tool that pushes encrypted per-host borg archives to
 a centralized backup server over SSH, driven by a per-host config in
 /etc/homelab/backup/client/ and run under systemd. General homelab
 disaster-recovery backup, not limited to /etc/homelab/* configs (see
 mode: in config.yml). Run `homelab-backup-client setup` after installing
 this package to set up config, encryption, and enrollment: the host's
 SSH pubkey is submitted to homelab-api once and applied automatically by
 homelab-backup-server's own reconciliation job -- no manual admin
 `enroll` command needed. Depends on homelab-cli for this and for
 optional run-history reporting; this package never talks to Postgres
 directly.
